ability":-0.27365511528731346,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.01638094628144332,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":33.6,"_gate_fund_growth":0.0985897878381869,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":98.6,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.019022075712534954,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":32.2,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.019466698067032495,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":74.3,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.05515708657440146,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":8.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.00408,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":2.7,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Skyworks Solutions, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, develops, manufactures, and markets analog and mixed-signal semiconductor products and solutions in the United States, Taiwan, China, South Korea, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and the Asia Pacific. The company offers amplifiers, antenna tuners, attenuators, automotive tuners and digital radios, wireless ASoC, DC/DC converters, demodulators, detectors, digital power isolators, diodes, directional couplers, diversity receive modules, filters, front-end modules, hybrids, light emitting diode drivers, low noise amplifiers, mixers, modulators, and optocouplers/optoisolators. It also provides phase locked loops, phase shifters, power dividers/combiners, power over ethernet, power isolators, ProSLIC family of subscriber line interface circuits, receivers, system in package, switches, synthesizers, timing devices, voltage-controlled oscillators/synthesizers, and voltage regulators. The company sells its products through direct sales force, electronic component distributors, and independent sales representatives. Its products are used in aerospace, automotive, broadband, cellular infrastructure, connected home, defense, entertainment and gaming, industrial, medical, smartphone, tablet, and wearables applications. The company was founded in 1962 and is headquartered in Irvine, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Philip Gordon Brace | CEO, President & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 10K people. Revenue per employee of $396K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 9%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $23K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $22K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Skyworks Solutions, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $21.1B market cap on $4.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -6% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 45%.","The business throws off $229M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.20\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 5.2\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.9%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 713% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":7.126235970448924},{"text":"Payout ratio of 187% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (13.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 10% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Skyworks Solutions, Inc. $SWKS Stock: Letko Brosseau & Associates Inc. Reduces Position","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/skyworks-solutions-inc-swks-stock-letko-brosseau-associates-inc-reduces-position.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794572199.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.917,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Skyworks Solutions, Inc.